Security Audit Tool

This tool is a simple script which gives information to the relevant personeel and users
who might run the script on  world writable files, users with no passwords, unsuccesful ssh logins
permission check on critical files, look into the ssh config, check the binaries that have SUID and SGID, 
make an aduit report on failed events, check upgradable packages, kernel errors, check
current running cron jobs, network interfaces information, processes run by root, password policies,
open sockets, and failed services; all of these that makes secuirty info on the system, thus the name security aduit tool.

Requirements

Root privileges - Some checks require sudo/root for complete results
For Debian based Linux distribution.

Usage

Open a terminal and make the script executable:

    chmod +x security_audit.sh

Execute with sudo for full results:

    sudo ./security_audit.sh           Show the banner and interactive menu
    sudo ./security_audit.sh --all     Run every check
    ./security_audit.sh --help         Show this README
    ./security_audit.sh --version      Show the version

Short forms are also accepted: -a or all, -h or help, -v or version.

Keep this README in the same directory as the script, because --help reads it
from there.
